# MapLink line-ending and diff policy.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Without it, ~130 files that nobody had touched showed as fully rewritten in
# every `git status`, because the working tree and the index disagreed about
# CRLF. A diff you cannot read is a diff nobody reviews, and the v1.20 drop was
# nearly submitted with its real changes buried in that noise.
#
# Source is stored AND checked out as LF. That is deliberate rather than
# leaving it to each machine's core.autocrlf: VS2022, Blender and every editor
# in this pipeline read LF fine, and pinning it means a file edited on one
# machine, or by a tool, cannot come back looking wholly rewritten on another.
#
# Batch files are the exception and MUST be CRLF: cmd.exe can mis-parse labels
# and goto in an LF-only .bat/.cmd, which fails at run time rather than at
# checkout, where it is much harder to attribute.

*               text=auto

# ── Source, pinned to LF ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.py            text eol=lf diff=python
*.cpp           text eol=lf diff=cpp
*.h             text eol=lf diff=cpp
*.cs            text eol=lf diff=csharp
*.uplugin       text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.ini           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.svg           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.gitignore     text eol=lf
*.gitattributes text eol=lf

# ── Windows batch, pinned to CRLF ─────────────────────────────────────
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.bat           text eol=crlf

# ── Binary: never normalised, never diffed as text ────────────────────
*.uasset        binary
*.umap          binary
*.blend         binary
*.blend1        binary
*.png           binary
*.tga           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.ico           binary
*.ai            binary
*.zip           binary
*.dll           binary
*.exe           binary
*.lib           binary
*.pdb           binary
*.pyc           binary
